cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this app, please cite the work it implements (preferred-citation), this release, and Pennsieve (RRID:SCR_021677); the other works it builds on are listed under references.
type: software
title: ophys-activity
abstract: 'Population analysis of calcium imaging data from NWB: activity summary (event rates), Rastermap-sorted
  population raster, pairwise correlations and cell assemblies (PCA/ICA after Lopes-dos-Santos et al. 2013) for any
  recording; with a stimulus or trials table also stimulus-aligned responses, responsiveness against a random-time
  null with FDR, tuning curves with orientation/direction selectivity (vector sum and peak indices) or a categorical
  selectivity index, trial-to-trial reliability, signal and noise correlations, sparseness, and a trials x ROIs response
  matrix for decoding. Part of the Pennsieve Two-photon Calcium Imaging workflow.'
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/ophys-activity
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
- neuroscience
- calcium-imaging
- two-photon
- nwb
- tuning
- orientation-selectivity
- noise-correlations
- cell-assemblies
- rastermap
# The work this app implements; the release report's "How to cite" puts it first.
